<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<worksheet xml:id="mth108-growth-patterns">
<title>Growth Patterns</title>
<objectives>
<ul>
<li>Given a visual pattern, I can draw the next case, record the number of shapes in a table, describe in my own words how the pattern grows, and plot the counts on a graph.</li>
</ul>
</objectives>

<introduction>
<p>For each pattern below: draw Case 4, complete the table, describe in your own words how the pattern grows, then plot the number of shapes for each case as a point on the grid.</p>
</introduction>

<page>
<exercise xml:id="gp-pattern-square">
<title>Pattern 1</title>
<introduction>
<p>The first three cases of a pattern of squares are shown below. Each case is a solid square of tiles.</p>
<image width="80%">
<shortdescription>Solid squares of tiles measuring one by one, two by two, and three by three, followed by a blank outline for Case 4.</shortdescription>
<description>
<p>A sequence of solid squares built from square tiles. Case 1 is a single tile. Case 2 is two tiles wide and two tiles tall, four tiles in all. Case 3 is three tiles wide and three tiles tall, nine tiles in all. Case 4 is shown as an empty outline four tiles wide and four tiles tall.</p>
</description>
<prefigure xmlns="https://prefigure.org" label="gp-square-pattern">
<diagram dimensions="(640,240)" margins="5">
<coordinates bbox="(-1,-1.7,15.5,4.6)">
<rectangle lower-left="(0,0)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="cornflowerblue" stroke="black"/>
<repeat parameter="i=0..1">
<repeat parameter="j=0..1">
<rectangle lower-left="(2.5+i,j)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="cornflowerblue" stroke="black"/>
</repeat>
</repeat>
<repeat parameter="i=0..2">
<repeat parameter="j=0..2">
<rectangle lower-left="(6+i,j)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="cornflowerblue" stroke="black"/>
</repeat>
</repeat>
<rectangle lower-left="(10.5,0)" dimensions="(3.9,3.9)" stroke="gray"/>
<label anchor="(0.45,-0.5)" alignment="south">Case 1</label>
<label anchor="(3.45,-0.5)" alignment="south">Case 2</label>
<label anchor="(7.45,-0.5)" alignment="south">Case 3</label>
<label anchor="(12.45,-0.5)" alignment="south">Case 4</label>
</coordinates>
</diagram>
</prefigure>
</image>
</introduction>

<task workspace="1.75in">
<statement>
<p>Draw Case 4.</p>
</statement>
</task>

<task>
<statement>
<p>Count the shapes in each case and complete the table.</p>
<tabular halign="center" top="minor" left="minor" bottom="minor" right="minor">
<row header="yes">
<cell>Case (<m>n</m>)</cell>
<cell><m>1</m></cell>
<cell><m>2</m></cell>
<cell><m>3</m></cell>
<cell><m>4</m></cell>
<cell><m>5</m></cell>
</row>
<row>
<cell>Shapes</cell>
<cell><m>1</m></cell>
<cell><m>4</m></cell>
<cell><m>9</m></cell>
<cell></cell>
<cell></cell>
</row>
</tabular>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>The counts are <m>1, 4, 9, 16, 25</m>.</p>
</answer>
</task>

<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>In your own words, describe how the pattern grows from one case to the next.</p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>Case <m>n</m> is a square that is <m>n</m> tiles wide and <m>n</m> tiles tall, so the number of tiles is <m>n</m> times <m>n</m>. Going from one case to the next, a new row is added along the bottom and a new column along the side, so the number of tiles added grows each time: <m>3</m> tiles from Case 1 to Case 2, then <m>5</m>, then <m>7</m>, then <m>9</m>.</p>
</answer>
</task>

<task>
<statement>
<p>Plot the number of shapes for each case as a point on the grid below.</p>
<image width="60%">
<shortdescription>An empty coordinate grid for plotting, with case number from 1 to 7 across and number of shapes from 0 to 26 up.</shortdescription>
<description>
<p>A blank coordinate grid. The horizontal axis is labeled Case number and is marked at each whole number from 1 to 7. The vertical axis is labeled Number of shapes and is marked every 2 units from 2 to 26.</p>
</description>
<prefigure xmlns="https://prefigure.org" label="gp-square-grid">
<diagram dimensions="(400,420)" margins="5">
<coordinates bbox="(-2,-4.6,8.4,28)">
<grid-axes hspacing="(0,1,7)" vspacing="(0,2,26)" hlabels="(1,1,7)" vlabels="(2,2,26)"/>
<label anchor="(4,-3.9)" alignment="center">Case number</label>
<label anchor="(-1.7,13)" alignment="center" rotate="90">Number of shapes</label>
</coordinates>
</diagram>
</prefigure>
</image>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>The points are <m>(1,1)</m>, <m>(2,4)</m>, <m>(3,9)</m>, <m>(4,16)</m>, and <m>(5,25)</m>. They do not fall in a straight line; the points climb more steeply with each case.</p>
</answer>
</task>
</exercise>
</page>

<page>
<exercise xml:id="gp-pattern-staircase">
<title>Pattern 2</title>
<introduction>
<p>The first three cases of a pattern are shown below. Each case is a staircase, built one row at a time.</p>
<image width="80%">
<shortdescription>Staircases of tiles containing one, three, and six tiles, followed by a blank outline for Case 4.</shortdescription>
<description>
<p>A sequence of staircases built from square tiles. Case 1 is a single tile. Case 2 has a bottom row of two tiles with one tile above the left tile, three tiles in all. Case 3 has a bottom row of three tiles, a row of two above it, and a single tile on top, six tiles in all. Case 4 is shown as an empty outline four tiles wide and four tiles tall.</p>
</description>
<prefigure xmlns="https://prefigure.org" label="gp-staircase-pattern">
<diagram dimensions="(640,240)" margins="5">
<coordinates bbox="(-1,-1.7,15.5,4.6)">
<rectangle lower-left="(0,0)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="lightseagreen" stroke="black"/>
<repeat parameter="i=0..1">
<rectangle lower-left="(2.5+i,0)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="lightseagreen" stroke="black"/>
</repeat>
<rectangle lower-left="(2.5,1)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="lightseagreen" stroke="black"/>
<repeat parameter="i=0..2">
<rectangle lower-left="(6+i,0)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="lightseagreen" stroke="black"/>
</repeat>
<repeat parameter="i=0..1">
<rectangle lower-left="(6+i,1)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="lightseagreen" stroke="black"/>
</repeat>
<rectangle lower-left="(6,2)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="lightseagreen" stroke="black"/>
<rectangle lower-left="(10.5,0)" dimensions="(3.9,3.9)" stroke="gray"/>
<label anchor="(0.45,-0.5)" alignment="south">Case 1</label>
<label anchor="(3.45,-0.5)" alignment="south">Case 2</label>
<label anchor="(7.45,-0.5)" alignment="south">Case 3</label>
<label anchor="(12.45,-0.5)" alignment="south">Case 4</label>
</coordinates>
</diagram>
</prefigure>
</image>
</introduction>

<task workspace="1.75in">
<statement>
<p>Draw Case 4.</p>
</statement>
</task>

<task>
<statement>
<p>Count the shapes in each case and complete the table.</p>
<tabular halign="center" top="minor" left="minor" bottom="minor" right="minor">
<row header="yes">
<cell>Case (<m>n</m>)</cell>
<cell><m>1</m></cell>
<cell><m>2</m></cell>
<cell><m>3</m></cell>
<cell><m>4</m></cell>
<cell><m>5</m></cell>
</row>
<row>
<cell>Shapes</cell>
<cell><m>1</m></cell>
<cell><m>3</m></cell>
<cell><m>6</m></cell>
<cell></cell>
<cell></cell>
</row>
</tabular>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>The counts are <m>1, 3, 6, 10, 15</m>.</p>
</answer>
</task>

<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>In your own words, describe how the pattern grows from one case to the next.</p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>Each case adds one more row along the bottom, and that new row has one more tile than the row that was on the bottom before. So Case 2 adds <m>2</m> tiles, Case 3 adds <m>3</m> tiles, Case 4 adds <m>4</m> tiles, and Case 5 adds <m>5</m> tiles. The number of tiles added grows by one each time.</p>
</answer>
</task>

<task>
<statement>
<p>Plot the number of shapes for each case as a point on the grid below.</p>
<image width="60%">
<shortdescription>An empty coordinate grid for plotting, with case number from 1 to 7 across and number of shapes from 0 to 16 up.</shortdescription>
<description>
<p>A blank coordinate grid. The horizontal axis is labeled Case number and is marked at each whole number from 1 to 7. The vertical axis is labeled Number of shapes and is marked every 2 units from 2 to 16.</p>
</description>
<prefigure xmlns="https://prefigure.org" label="gp-staircase-grid">
<diagram dimensions="(400,330)" margins="5">
<coordinates bbox="(-2,-3.2,8.4,17.6)">
<grid-axes hspacing="(0,1,7)" vspacing="(0,2,16)" hlabels="(1,1,7)" vlabels="(2,2,16)"/>
<label anchor="(4,-2.6)" alignment="center">Case number</label>
<label anchor="(-1.7,8)" alignment="center" rotate="90">Number of shapes</label>
</coordinates>
</diagram>
</prefigure>
</image>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>The points are <m>(1,1)</m>, <m>(2,3)</m>, <m>(3,6)</m>, <m>(4,10)</m>, and <m>(5,15)</m>. They do not fall in a straight line; each step up is a little larger than the one before.</p>
</answer>
</task>
</exercise>
</page>

<page>
<exercise xml:id="gp-pattern-row">
<title>Pattern 3</title>
<introduction>
<p>The first three cases of a pattern are shown below. Each case is a single row of tiles.</p>
<image width="90%">
<shortdescription>Single rows of tiles containing one, two, and four tiles, followed by a blank outline for Case 4.</shortdescription>
<description>
<p>A sequence of single rows built from square tiles. Case 1 is one tile. Case 2 is a row of two tiles. Case 3 is a row of four tiles. Case 4 is shown as an empty outline eight tiles long.</p>
</description>
<prefigure xmlns="https://prefigure.org" label="gp-row-pattern">
<diagram dimensions="(640,110)" margins="5">
<coordinates bbox="(-1,-1.7,21,2.4)">
<rectangle lower-left="(0,0)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="plum" stroke="black"/>
<repeat parameter="i=0..1">
<rectangle lower-left="(2.5+i,0)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="plum" stroke="black"/>
</repeat>
<repeat parameter="i=0..3">
<rectangle lower-left="(6+i,0)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="plum" stroke="black"/>
</repeat>
<rectangle lower-left="(11.5,0)" dimensions="(7.9,0.9)" stroke="gray"/>
<label anchor="(0.45,-0.5)" alignment="south">Case 1</label>
<label anchor="(3.45,-0.5)" alignment="south">Case 2</label>
<label anchor="(7.95,-0.5)" alignment="south">Case 3</label>
<label anchor="(15.45,-0.5)" alignment="south">Case 4</label>
</coordinates>
</diagram>
</prefigure>
</image>
</introduction>

<task workspace="1.25in">
<statement>
<p>Draw Case 4.</p>
</statement>
</task>

<task>
<statement>
<p>Count the shapes in each case and complete the table.</p>
<tabular halign="center" top="minor" left="minor" bottom="minor" right="minor">
<row header="yes">
<cell>Case (<m>n</m>)</cell>
<cell><m>1</m></cell>
<cell><m>2</m></cell>
<cell><m>3</m></cell>
<cell><m>4</m></cell>
<cell><m>5</m></cell>
</row>
<row>
<cell>Shapes</cell>
<cell><m>1</m></cell>
<cell><m>2</m></cell>
<cell><m>4</m></cell>
<cell></cell>
<cell></cell>
</row>
</tabular>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>The counts are <m>1, 2, 4, 8, 16</m>.</p>
</answer>
</task>

<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>In your own words, describe how the pattern grows from one case to the next.</p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>Each case has twice as many tiles as the case before it. The row doubles in length every time, so the number of tiles added also doubles: <m>1</m> tile is added, then <m>2</m>, then <m>4</m>, then <m>8</m>.</p>
</answer>
</task>

<task>
<statement>
<p>Plot the number of shapes for each case as a point on the grid below.</p>
<image width="60%">
<shortdescription>An empty coordinate grid for plotting, with case number from 1 to 7 across and number of shapes from 0 to 16 up.</shortdescription>
<description>
<p>A blank coordinate grid. The horizontal axis is labeled Case number and is marked at each whole number from 1 to 7. The vertical axis is labeled Number of shapes and is marked every 2 units from 2 to 16.</p>
</description>
<prefigure xmlns="https://prefigure.org" label="gp-row-grid">
<diagram dimensions="(400,330)" margins="5">
<coordinates bbox="(-2,-3.2,8.4,17.6)">
<grid-axes hspacing="(0,1,7)" vspacing="(0,2,16)" hlabels="(1,1,7)" vlabels="(2,2,16)"/>
<label anchor="(4,-2.6)" alignment="center">Case number</label>
<label anchor="(-1.7,8)" alignment="center" rotate="90">Number of shapes</label>
</coordinates>
</diagram>
</prefigure>
</image>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>The points are <m>(1,1)</m>, <m>(2,2)</m>, <m>(3,4)</m>, <m>(4,8)</m>, and <m>(5,16)</m>. They do not fall in a straight line; the points stay low at first and then climb very quickly.</p>
</answer>
</task>
</exercise>
</page>

<page>
<exercise xml:id="gp-pattern-plus">
<title>Pattern 4</title>
<introduction>
<p>The first three cases of a pattern are shown below. Each case is a plus sign with four arms.</p>
<image width="80%">
<shortdescription>Plus signs built from tiles containing five, nine, and thirteen tiles, followed by a blank outline for Case 4.</shortdescription>
<description>
<p>A sequence of plus signs built from square tiles. Case 1 is a center tile with one tile out from each of the four sides, five tiles in all. Case 2 has arms two tiles long, nine tiles in all. Case 3 has arms three tiles long, thirteen tiles in all. Case 4 is shown as an empty outline nine tiles wide and nine tiles tall.</p>
</description>
<prefigure xmlns="https://prefigure.org" label="gp-plus-pattern">
<diagram dimensions="(640,250)" margins="5">
<coordinates bbox="(-1,-2,28.5,9.9)">
<repeat parameter="i=0..2">
<rectangle lower-left="(i,1)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="lightcoral" stroke="black"/>
</repeat>
<rectangle lower-left="(1,0)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="lightcoral" stroke="black"/>
<rectangle lower-left="(1,2)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="lightcoral" stroke="black"/>
<repeat parameter="i=0..4">
<rectangle lower-left="(4.5+i,2)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="lightcoral" stroke="black"/>
</repeat>
<repeat parameter="j=0..1">
<rectangle lower-left="(6.5,j)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="lightcoral" stroke="black"/>
</repeat>
<repeat parameter="j=3..4">
<rectangle lower-left="(6.5,j)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="lightcoral" stroke="black"/>
</repeat>
<repeat parameter="i=0..6">
<rectangle lower-left="(11.5+i,3)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="lightcoral" stroke="black"/>
</repeat>
<repeat parameter="j=0..2">
<rectangle lower-left="(14.5,j)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="lightcoral" stroke="black"/>
</repeat>
<repeat parameter="j=4..6">
<rectangle lower-left="(14.5,j)" dimensions="(0.9,0.9)" fill="lightcoral" stroke="black"/>
</repeat>
<rectangle lower-left="(19.5,0)" dimensions="(8.9,8.9)" stroke="gray"/>
<label anchor="(1.45,-0.8)" alignment="south">Case 1</label>
<label anchor="(6.95,-0.8)" alignment="south">Case 2</label>
<label anchor="(14.95,-0.8)" alignment="south">Case 3</label>
<label anchor="(23.95,-0.8)" alignment="south">Case 4</label>
</coordinates>
</diagram>
</prefigure>
</image>
</introduction>

<task workspace="2in">
<statement>
<p>Draw Case 4.</p>
</statement>
</task>

<task>
<statement>
<p>Count the shapes in each case and complete the table.</p>
<tabular halign="center" top="minor" left="minor" bottom="minor" right="minor">
<row header="yes">
<cell>Case (<m>n</m>)</cell>
<cell><m>1</m></cell>
<cell><m>2</m></cell>
<cell><m>3</m></cell>
<cell><m>4</m></cell>
<cell><m>5</m></cell>
</row>
<row>
<cell>Shapes</cell>
<cell><m>5</m></cell>
<cell><m>9</m></cell>
<cell><m>13</m></cell>
<cell></cell>
<cell></cell>
</row>
</tabular>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>The counts are <m>5, 9, 13, 17, 21</m>.</p>
</answer>
</task>

<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>In your own words, describe how the pattern grows from one case to the next.</p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>Each case adds one tile to the end of each of the four arms, so <m>4</m> tiles are added every time. The center tile stays the same throughout.</p>
</answer>
</task>

<task>
<statement>
<p>Plot the number of shapes for each case as a point on the grid below.</p>
<image width="60%">
<shortdescription>An empty coordinate grid for plotting, with case number from 1 to 7 across and number of shapes from 0 to 22 up.</shortdescription>
<description>
<p>A blank coordinate grid. The horizontal axis is labeled Case number and is marked at each whole number from 1 to 7. The vertical axis is labeled Number of shapes and is marked every 2 units from 2 to 22.</p>
</description>
<prefigure xmlns="https://prefigure.org" label="gp-plus-grid">
<diagram dimensions="(400,380)" margins="5">
<coordinates bbox="(-2,-4,8.4,23.8)">
<grid-axes hspacing="(0,1,7)" vspacing="(0,2,22)" hlabels="(1,1,7)" vlabels="(2,2,22)"/>
<label anchor="(4,-3.3)" alignment="center">Case number</label>
<label anchor="(-1.7,11)" alignment="center" rotate="90">Number of shapes</label>
</coordinates>
</diagram>
</prefigure>
</image>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>The points are <m>(1,5)</m>, <m>(2,9)</m>, <m>(3,13)</m>, <m>(4,17)</m>, and <m>(5,21)</m>. These points do fall in a straight line, since the same number of tiles is added each time.</p>
</answer>
</task>

<task workspace="1.25in">
<statement>
<p>How many shapes would be in Case 10? Explain how you figured it out.</p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>There would be <m>41</m> shapes. Case 5 has <m>21</m> tiles, and each case after that adds <m>4</m> more, so Cases 6 through 10 have <m>25, 29, 33, 37</m>, and <m>41</m> tiles. Another way to see it: each arm in Case 10 is <m>10</m> tiles long, which accounts for <m>4 \cdot 10 = 40</m> tiles, plus the <m>1</m> center tile the arms share, giving <m>41</m>.</p>
</answer>
</task>
</exercise>
</page>

</worksheet>
